  "_comment": "IAW actuator tests (InputOutputControlByLocalIdentifier). Command: 30 <localid> 07 (activate) / 30 <localid> 00 (deactivate); positive response SID 0x70. LocalID->name from JPDiag28c.ini [Tests]; command byte 07/00 cross-confirmed from the GuzziDiag v0.61 reverse. This is the full IAW set (car + bike); a 2-cylinder Guzzi 5AM only has some of these physically (coils 1/2, injectors 1/2, fuel pump, tacho, stepper, O2 heaters, purge, warning lamp) — the rest simply NRC on that ECU. Momentary pulse (auto-deactivate) by default. WARNING: these energize real outputs (fuel/spark/pump) — engine off, ignition on. LocalID 0x20 (32) is NOT in the JPDiag [Tests] list: it was found in the IAWDiag family that carries the same 5AM actuator set (30 20 07), and the GuzziDiag 5AM button 'Leerlaufregelung' (View_61, dword_45D7F8 = sub_427BCF) has no body in the dump — 0x20 is the likely idle-control it drives. Unverified: listed with the '*' marker.",
